# RoadFix - Supabase Configuration (Phase 2A: Backend Foundation)
# In Phase 2A, the frontend remains decoupled; no backend is actively connected.
# When connecting to Supabase in subsequent phases, copy this file to .env and provide your values.
#
# SECURITY RULES:
# 1. Provide ONLY your Supabase project URL and the public anon/publishable key.
# 2. NEVER put a service-role key, secret key, or database password in any VITE_ variable or client environment file.
# 3. All VITE_ variables are bundled into client-side JavaScript and are publicly readable by anyone.
# 4. Never commit .env files into version control.

# The public URL of your Supabase instance (e.g. https://your-project-id.supabase.co or http://127.0.0.1:54321)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The public anon / publishable key for your Supabase project (safe for client-side usage; NEVER use service_role)
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
